    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d944">

                <pb facs="1005" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/4135</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >McAdoo</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-09-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 21, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith a
                    copy of a letter dated the 20th instant from the collector of customs at New
                    York, N. Y., relative to certain alterations which are in progress on the
                    British steamships <hi rendition="#italic">Laconia</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tuscania</hi>.</p>
                <p>I will thank you to advise me what instructions you desire given to the collector
                    in the matter. Attention is invited to the collector’s statement that the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Laconia</hi> is to sail on Friday and the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tuscania</hi> on Saturday, and that the steamship
                    company therefore requests an early decision.</p>
                <p>By direction of the Secretary.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">James L. Wilmeth</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Assistant Secretary</hi>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d944-a1.xml" xpointer="d944-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
